// Language section: Interfaces.
page interfaces { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Interfaces"

  p "An `interface` declares a structural contract — a set of fields a type must have to satisfy it. Any type with the right fields satisfies it automatically, no explicit `implements`."

  h2 "Declaring an interface"

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
interface Drawable {
  x: f64
  y: f64
}

interface Sized extends Drawable {
  width:  f64
  height: f64
}
WCL
  }

  callout "Structural, not nominal" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "A type does not need to be declared as a parent or to implement anything explicitly. If it happens to have all the interface's fields with compatible types, it satisfies the interface."
  }

  p "Interfaces have one common consumer: **reference fields** (`&T`), which accept any value that structurally satisfies the interface. That's what the next chapter covers."
}
